  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nPOSTPONED: Kinder | Show Time: 7pm | Date: 16 June 2026\n£15.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nKinder\n\nEVENT POSTPONED - PLEASE NOTE: This event and other show times originally scheduled for June 2026 have been postponed due to cast and crew illness. Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum and Smoking Apples apologise for the inconvenience caused, and we hope to provide a new set of show times later in the year (targeting September/October 2026) when the crew are back to full strength.\n\nIf you have already booked tickets to this or any other date, you will be contacted shortly regarding refunds. If you have booked and have not received any contact from us, please get in touch via frontofhouse@sofo.org.uk. (UPDATED 11:25 30/05/2026)\n\n----\n\nOriginal listing:\nShow Time: 7pm, 16 June 2026\n\n(This show time is intended for anyone, if you are interested in booking a school group, please check our other show times, or contact us for group ticket pricing)\n\nEscaping on a Kindertransport train, one small Czech-Jewish girl embarks on a mighty adventure.\n\nCrossing between the past and present, Babi travels across Europe; from bon bons in Germany to the smell of the sea in Margate, she discovers how tiny acts of kindness can change the course of a person’s life.\n\nJoyful, moving and poignant, Kinder features beautiful table-top puppetry and cinematic shadow play, as Babi tries to assemble the parts of her broken identity, to find peace in her future.\n\nKinder is a multi-award winning show, from puppetry and visual theatre company Smoking Apples. Inviting you to take a seat inside an immersive set, the story unfolds through a series of playful hatches and openings.\n\n“Unmissable” – ✮✮✮✮✮ Everything Theatre\n\nA Smoking Apples production, aimed at ages 9 - 18 years.\n\nSupported using public funding by the National Lottery through Arts Council England and Enterprise Arts Trust.\n\n---\nAwards for Smoking Apples' Kinder:\n\nOFFIE Winner for Theatre for Young Audiences – Original Music/Sound 2023\nOFFIE Winner for Theatre for Young Audiences – Production 2023\nOFFIE Finalist for Theatre for Young audiences – Writing – 2023\nEttie Award Winner for Best Theatre for Young Audiences Production – 2023\n---\nVenue: Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum, Park Street, Woodstock, OX20 1SN\n\nShows take place in our Briefing Room events space, open-plan with our Main Gallery.\n\nRunning time: 55 minutes (no interval).\n\n--\nAge Suitability\n\nKinder is best suited to ages 9 +. The show is ideal for ages 9 - 18, with ages 9 - 11 (Years 5 & 6) learning about the Holocaust, as part of the curriculum and ages 12 - 18 (Years 7 - 13) studying Drama, English, History and/or Religious Studies.\n\nThe show contains some complex references to war and persecution, which younger audiences may find challenging. Kinder runs for up to an hour, without an interval and for the duration, the audience are seated\n\nAccessibility\n\nKinder has been designed to be accessible for neurodivergent audiences. In the space, we will be providing stims (stimulatory accessories) and active responses to the show are encouraged. Audiences will be able to leave and re-enter the show, at any time and there will be a chill out area (with bean bags, ear defenders and more stims) for periods of regulation. An inclusive resource pack is available on the Smoking Apples thetre website in advance and includes a social story. Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum also has its own social story available on our Visit Us page.\n\nThe show and venue is wheelchair accessible, providing that we are informed in advance so that we can take into account the seating arrangement and adjust audience numbers accordingly.\n\n--\n\nDate: 16-June-2026\nTime: 19:00\n\nLocation: Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum (The Briefing Room, Main Gallery), Park Street, Woodstock, OX20 1SN\nType: digital\n\nRelated products\nMeet Me at the Soldiers Museum | 2pm – 4pm | Thursday 25 June 2026\n£0.00 Add to cart\nWomen at War with Kate Vigurs | 7pm, 19 August 2026\n£15.00 Add to cart\nMeet Me at the Soldiers Museum | 2pm – 4pm | Thursday 9 July 2026\n£0.00 Add to cart\nWoodstock’s Last Night of the Proms | St Mary Magdalene Church | 7pm 26 September 2026\n£12.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
